  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "For subsets $A$ and $B$ of a set $X$, define the set $A*B$ as $A*B=(A\\cap B)\\cup((X-A)\\cap(X-B))$. Then only one of the following statements is true. Which one is it?",
  "options": {
    "A": "$A*(X-B)\\subset A*B$ and $A*(X-B)\\ne A*B$",
    "B": "$A*B=A*(X-B)$",
    "C": "$A*B\\subset A*(X-B)$ and $A*B\\ne A*(X-B)$",
    "D": "$X-(A*B)=A*(X-B)$"
  },
  "answer": "D",
